        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Textile, tray cover, silk, gold wire, applied gold-wrapped thread, Madras, ca. 1855"@en , "Intended for use as a cover."@en , "Circular tray cover, the ground is made of flattened gold wire, over which are appliquéd a central field with floral designs in gold-wrapped thread and sequins, surrounded by a band of flowers made up of red and green spangles on a fringe of flattened gold wire. With a single central floral motif, composed of gold sequins and gold-wrapped thread. Backed with crimson silk."@en ;
